00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.090
Abraham: Most people today carry a smart
phone, it is a way of communicating

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.800
with friends, watching and downloading
movies and TV series, catching up on news

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.199
stories, buying things online and booking
tickets for a range of different things.

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.540
It can also be used for playing games
and communicating with a variety

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.260
of other devices and appliances
around the home and at work.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.729
For some people it is their only point of
contact as they no longer have a landline.

00:00:33.459 --> 00:00:36.580
Nicole: There are lots of positives
for having a smart phone but there are

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.360
negatives that we have to consider.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:44.350
As the number of mobile phone users around
the world soars mobile networks need to be

00:00:44.350 --> 00:00:49.320
able to handle the immense demands on data
and how quickly they can access services.

00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:54.229
The opportunity for cybercrime
increases as our dependency increases.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.510
Mobile malware can target systems
due to unsecure usage of URL's

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.569
over WiFi or other networks.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.329
Mobile users are at risk of spam
and other cybersecurity attacks.

00:01:06.639 --> 00:01:10.690
We all know about those bogus SMS
messages asking us to click on a link.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.220
Abraham: Let's start by looking
at the hype around 5G fifth

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.750
generation wireless network.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.200
3G smartphones have download speeds
of approximately 2Mbps [megabits

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.980
per second], 4G is around 3-5Mbps.

00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:31.190
Currently 5G is at least 3-6 times faster
than 4G but could reach up to 100-200Mbps

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:36.830
but this will depend on the providers
coverage and the areas a person is in.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:42.059
As mobile network generations evolve
the speed and efficiency increases

00:01:42.059 --> 00:01:47.660
and offers a great more opportunities
for connectivity and the use of IOT.

00:01:48.629 --> 00:01:51.950
5G means gadgets will be more
efficient and therefore relied on

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.440
more but they will also be more
opportunities for cyber attacks.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:00.520
There is also a lot of opposition to 5G
and conspiracy theories are increasing.

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:04.200
This opens opportunities for
anti 5G activists and a great

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.459
deal of false information.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:10.449
Nicole: This level of connectivity
will be and to some extent is already

00:02:10.449 --> 00:02:15.510
all around us, imagine fully connected
homes, vehicles and smart cities.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:21.230
With this new connectivity and the
use of IOT devices, cyber security

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.060
is even more essential, as we rely
on this technology more, then the

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.160
need for it to be secure is greater.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:31.320
Allowing devices to connect to
the internet opens them up to a

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.929
number of serious vulnerabilities
if they are not protected properly.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:40.570
Application programme interface
or API security and public key

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:45.090
infrastructure, PKI authentication
are a few of the methods that can

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:46.770
be used to combat this threat.

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:51.459
Imagine if an electric car was
hacked what damage could be caused,

00:02:51.719 --> 00:02:55.180
we have all seen this portrayed
in movies but it is a real threat.

00:02:55.809 --> 00:02:59.929
Household devices run off the local area
networks and should be covered by the

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:04.930
router or hub's firewall security, but
mobile devices are a different matter.

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:10.240
It is all too easy for cyber criminals
to clone phones and credit card details

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.630
by just passing close to an individual.

